    "answer": {
      "short": "$P(A\\mid B)=0$, since mutual exclusivity gives $P(A\\cap B)=0$.",
      "worked": "Mutually exclusive events have $A\\cap B=\\varnothing$, so $P(A\\cap B)=0$. Since $P(B)>0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A\\mid B)&=\\frac{P(A\\cap B)}{P(B)}\\\\P(A\\mid B)&=\\frac{0}{P(B)}\\\\P(A\\mid B)&=0.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
